.TH PWM 3
.SH NAME
pwm \- pulse-width modulation, as files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B bind -a #W /dev

.BI /dev/pwm N
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pwm
serves the four channels of the Raspberry Pi 5's PWM0, on GPIO 12, 13, 18
and 19.
Times are in nanoseconds, in steps of 20, to 85 seconds.
A write to a channel holds any of
.BI period " ns" ,
.BI duty " ns" ,
.B on
and
.BR off ;
a read returns them.
A pin becomes PWM's at
.BR on ,
and one in use by something else refuses:
GPIO 12 and 13 are the kernel's second console.
.SH SOURCE
.B /os/bcm2712/devpwm.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR gpio (3),
.IR spi (3)
